        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@oncomouse, this is now possible with the `vis_mode` field in returned region table. The following `custom_textobjects` specification should work now as you'd expect (tested with [vim-sort-motion](https://github.com/christoomey/vim-sort-motion)):\r\n```lua\r\ne = function() -- Whole buffer\r\n  local from = { line = 1, col = 1 }\r\n  local last_line_length = #vim.fn.getline('$')\r\n  local to = {\r\n    line = vim.fn.line('$'),\r\n    col = last_line_length == 0 and 1 or last_line_length,\r\n  }\r\n  return { from = from, to = to, vis_mode = 'V' }\r\nend,\r\n```\r\n\r\n(Side note: I almost closed this without adding new feature because forcing selection mode still works. So with your original textobject specification, doing `gsVae` worked. See `:h forced-motion`)",
            "created_at": "2023-06-29T13:25:15Z",
